# CANONICAL §7.6 fixture — `ProjectToSketchPlane` (WP-P, 2026-09-02): project
# picked body edges, or a picked face's whole boundary, into the ACTIVE sketch's
# plane. The verb Rust commits as reference-locked sketch geometry.
#
# SELF-GENERATING. Four bodies are built from integer sketches in one plan, then a
# 3 mm fillet is applied in a second, so the whole input is reproducible from this
# file alone and no binary is tracked. NOTE the worker's `plane:{"kind":"XY"}`
# convention (`SketchPlane::XY()`): user X maps to world +Y and user Y to world
# −X, so a world point (X,Y) is authored below as the sketch pair (Y, −X). That is
# why the squares read `[[0,0],[0,-20],[20,-20],[20,0]]` and land on the world
# square x,y ∈ [0,20]. Every PROJECTED number in the rounds is in world/plane UV.
#
# WHAT IS PINNED HERE, AND WHAT DELIBERATELY IS NOT.
#
# Pinned: every value that is an integer or an exactly-representable consequence
# of the construction — the box outline's four corners, the cylinder cap's
# `radius: 10.0` and centre `[50,0]`, the edge-on chord's `[40,20]`/`[60,20]`, the
# tilted ellipse's `majorR: 10.0`, the fillet arc's `radius: 3.0` and `ccw` — plus
# every branch a reader takes: the entity `type`, the `sourceRef` echo, the four
# refusal codes reachable from a built body here (`trimmedTiltedArc`,
# `unsupportedCurve`, `absent`, `kindMismatch`), and the fenced error. The other
# two — `degenerate` and `faceNotPlanar` — need shapes no plan can build, and are
# pinned in test_edge_projector.cpp against self-built OCCT geometry.
#
# NOT pinned: `minorR`, `rotation`, the tilted centre's v, and the arc's angles.
# They are irrational or measurement-shaped, and `json_subset` compares numbers
# EXACTLY — NDJSON is the wrong instrument for a value allowed to move by less
# than a nanometre. Their pins live in `worker/tests/test_edge_projector.cpp`
# (minorR = r·cosθ at three θ, the rotation values, the sliver threshold), the
# same contract/corpus split `analyze_edge_op_range` uses.
#
# `projectedHash` is NEVER pinned to a literal, only `$hex64`. It is FNV-1a over a
# 1e-6 quantization of doubles OCCT and libm produce, and a frozen digest would
# gate the platform instead of the contract (worker/tests/CMakeLists.txt:752-756
# gives the same reason for the profile bytes).
#
# ARRAY LENGTHS. `json_subset` is a SUBSET match over arrays: listing one entry
# asserts "at least one", and an expected `[]` asserts only "this key is an array".
# So the `"entities":[]` on the refusal rounds pins the response SHAPE (every
# branch answers the same key set, so Rust parses one shape) and NOT emptiness.
# The exact counts — "no entity was emitted for a refused source", "exactly one
# refusal" — are asserted in test_edge_projector.cpp, which can see the parsed
# result. Do not read a bare `[]` here as a length assertion.
#
# THE READ-ONLY GUARANTEE is asserted structurally: `GetWorkerHead` brackets every
# round and must be IDENTICAL field for field. This verb takes a head COPY — no
# scratch, no snapshot, no minting, no `bodyEvents`, no bin tail.
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"hello","seq":0}}
{"send":{"v":1,"t":"req","id":1,"verb":"OpenSession","args":{"documentId":"doc_project_to_sketch_plane","documentRevision":0,"workerEpoch":4,"mode":"determinism"}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"resp","id":1,"ok":true,"result":{"sessionOpen":true}}}
